    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345-a10">

                <pb facs="0618" n="490" xml:id="pg490"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 10 in No. 702.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Langston to Mr. St. Victor</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port-au-Prince, Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-01-14"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 14,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In acknowledging the receipt of your
                    dispatch of the 27th of last month, having relation to the affair of Mr. C. A.
                    Van Bokkelen, I have the honor to advise you that I await impatiently the
                    response which you therein promise to make to my dispatch addressed to you on
                    the 22d of December, 1884.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, Mr. Minister, to let me hear from you without further delay.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MERCER LANGSTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
